# AgilePlace CLI Usage Rule

**When to Apply**: Any time the user requests interaction with AgilePlace — creating cards, updating cards, fetching card details, listing cards from boards, managing lanes, planning increments, running reports, etc.

## MANDATORY: Use AgilePlace CLI

When the user asks to interact with AgilePlace, you MUST use the AgilePlace CLI rather than direct API calls or web automation.

### CLI Location
```
🔧 Automation/scripts/agileplace_cli/
```

### Invocation

**Preferred** (from within the scripts directory):
```bash
cd "🔧 Automation/scripts"
python -m agileplace_cli.cli <command>
```

**Also works** (backward compatible):
```bash
cd "🔧 Automation/scripts"
python agileplace_cli/cli.py <command>
```

**Or** (from workspace root, with PYTHONPATH):
```bash
PYTHONPATH="🔧 Automation/scripts" python "🔧 Automation/scripts/agileplace_cli/cli.py" <command>
```

## Available Commands (16 groups, 80+ commands)

### Authentication (`auth`)
```bash
agileplace auth whoami              # Check current user / verify auth
agileplace auth whoami --format table
agileplace auth check               # Exit 0 if valid, 1 if not
```

### Boards (`boards`)
